 <h3>4. #UI around an expression without assignment - errors in UI mode</h3>
 <p>Expected error: "The #UI keyword requires a variable assignment."</p>
 <p>
 </p>
 <p class="err">
  Error in "#UI {"type": "entry"}" on line [
  <a data-text="108" href="#0">108</a>
  ]: The #UI keyword requires a variable assignment.
 </p>
 <p>
 </p>
 <p>
 </p>
 <h3>5. #UI assigned an expression rather than a value - errors in both modes</h3>
 <p>
  Expected error: "#UI directives do not support expressions." A control overwrites the
  <p>right hand side with whatever was entered, so only a value, a vector or a matrix can be</p>
  <p>annotated. Reported by the linter as well.</p>
 </p>
 <p>
 </p>
 <p class="err">
  Error in "#UI {"type": "entry"} k = max(E2)" on line [
  <a data-text="115" href="#0">115</a>
  ]: #UI directives do not support expressions.
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>k</var>
   =
   <b>max</b>
   (
   <var>E2</var>
   )  =
   <b>max</b>
   ( 200
   <i>GPa</i>
   )  = 200
   <i>GPa</i>
  </span>
 </p>
 <p class="err">
  Error in "#UI {"type": "entry"} k2 = 2*E2" on line [
  <a data-text="116" href="#0">116</a>
  ]: #UI directives do not support expressions.
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>k2</var>
   = 2 ·
   <var>E2</var>
   = 2 · 200
   <i>GPa</i>
   = 400
   <i>GPa</i>
  </span>
 </p>
 <p class="err">
  Error in "#UI k3 = [1; sqrt(4)]" on line [
  <a data-text="117" href="#0">117</a>
  ]: #UI directives do not support expressions.
 </p>
 <p>
  <span class="eq">
   <var>
    <span class="vec">⃗</span>
    k3
   </var>
   =
   <span class="b0">[</span>
